{
  "manufacturer": "Intesis (HMS Networks)",
  "manufacturer_slug": "intesis",
  "model": "INMBSPAN001A100 Panasonic Aquarea H/J/K/L/M air-to-water to Modbus RTU gateway",
  "model_slug": "inmbspan001a100",
  "short_model": "INMBSPAN001A100",
  "aliases": [
    "INMBSPAN001A100",
    "Aquarea Modbus",
    "Panasonic Aquarea Modbus RTU",
    "Intesis Aquarea",
    "INMBSPAN001A000 (legacy order code)"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Heat pump gateway (VRF / split AC gateway)",
  "applies_to": "Intesis (HMS Networks) INMBSPAN001A100 gateway connected to Panasonic Aquarea H, J, K, L and M series air-to-water heat pumps, per user manual version 1.0.2 (2026-02-04).",
  "summary": "This Intesis interface connects to a Panasonic Aquarea hydro unit and presents it as a Modbus RTU server. All points are single 16-bit holding registers: system on/off and operating mode, zone setpoints and actual temperatures, DHW tank on/off and setpoint, water temperatures, present power draw, error code, unit configuration, and requests such as powerful, quiet and sterilisation. Some registers apply only to newer K/L/M series units.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Each register is listed with a 'Modbus address (base 0)' (protocol address) and a 'PLC address (base 1)'. This map uses the base-0 value as the wire address: System on/off is address 0 (PLC 1)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "INMBSPAN001A100 User Manual - Panasonic Aquarea H/J/K/L/M Air-to-Water Units to Modbus RTU",
    "doc_number": "User Manual Version 1.0.2",
    "revision_date": "2026-02-04",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/inmbspan001a100-user-manual-v1-0-0-en.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 7 (DIP switches), p. 13 (physical layer, functions, invalid values), pp. 14-29 (register tables), p. 30 (temperature register logic), p. 31 (error codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The download link's file name says v1-0-0 but the PDF it serves is version 1.0.2 dated 2026-02-04; the addresses here are from 1.0.2.",
    "Temperatures follow DIP switch SW4: P1 ON = tenths of a degree (x10, Celsius only), P2 ON = Fahrenheit; both OFF (factory) = whole °C. Units and scale here are for the default; use scale 0.1 if x10 is set.",
    "Temperature ranges go below zero (-127 to 127 °C), so temperatures are typed signed 16-bit. Invalid readings are 0x8000 on signed registers and 0xFFFF on unsigned ones.",
    "What register 12/13 (zone setpoint) and 14/15 (actual) mean depends on zone setup (83/84), setting mode (16/17) and operating mode (4): room, water, water shift or pool; see the table on p. 30.",
    "For registers whose values are range-checked, an out-of-range write is moved to the nearest limit (writing 6 to a 0-5 register applies 5).",
    "Left out: the 32-bit energy totals 120-131 and 366-373 (two registers each, word order not stated); compressor total on time 184-185 (split into MSB/LSB registers with a 24-bit range, packing not stated); the compensation-curve, bivalent, SG Ready capacity and M-series-only settings (150-438) - read them from the manual if needed."
  ],
